    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 142313\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n415 PM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the\n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Persistent troughing across the Western US will keep\nthe region in a generally dry and breezy pattern through much of\nthe upcoming week. In the near term, a trough will eject into the\nNorthern Plains today before additional troughing drops south\nalong the Pacific Northwest Coast by midweek. This will keep the\nMojave Desert and southern Great Basin region in a southwesterly\nflow aloft, favoring breezy conditions in the afternoons and any\nlingering monsoonal moisture focused more across central and\neastern Arizona. A few isolated thunderstorms may develop across\neastern Mohave County through midweek, but coverage is expected \nto be quite limited. \n\nOtherwise, thanks to the pattern at hand, temperatures will remain\nnear seasonal normals through the period. The flow pattern will\ntrend more zonal by the weekend allowing for the gusty winds to\nease while temperatures remain near normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...\nOverall normal daily summertime wind pattern expected through the \nTAF period with breezy afternoon and evenings and lighter winds at \nnight. SW winds 10-15kt with gusts 20-25kt continue through around \nsunset this evening, then gusts drop off for the overnight hours \nwhile S-SW winds diminish to 08-10kt. Brief period of SE-S winds \nexpected around 16z before a quick wind shift to S-SW 10-15kt with \nisolated gusts over 25kt at times during the afternoon Tuesday. by \nVFR conditions prevail, with temperatures briefly reaching a high of \n100 degrees around 23Z-00Z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Overall daily wind \npatterns expected at most sites through the TAF period, with a few \nexceptions. For the rest of today, S-SW winds with gusts 20-25kt \ncontinue through sunset then diminish some for the overnight hours. \nGuidance shows the potential for elevated winds near 10-12kt \novernight with isolated higher gusts at KIFP and KEED. KBIH is also \nan exception as winds have been light and VRB much of the day. \nExpect a brief period of SE-S winds through sunset, then a shift \ntoward light NW flow tonight. Higher confidence does exist in \nstronger SE-S winds 10-15kt with gusts to 25kt at KBIH during the \nafternoon and evening Tuesday. KDAG remains light and VRB out of the \nNE, but expect the daily WSW push to occur 00z-02z and persist \nthrough 09-10z. VFR conditions will prevail, with isolated \nthunderstorms expected over portions of northwestern Arizona this \nafternoon that are unlikely to cause any impacts at area terminals.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler \nAVIATION...Moore\n\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
